  "normalVisualFindings": {
    "neutral": "Recognizable small flycatcher stance with dark warm-brown head/back, pale belly, narrow bill and longish tail; holds steady in both source and codec versions. Historical warm-brown/pale-edge plumage limitation remains, not newly corrected here.",
    "blink": "Open eye highlight/eye shape changes to a short darker closed-eye cue. Brief and small at91world, but source and binary version retain the closure cue without a new bright false eye spot. Body/feet minor native redraw remains; provisional usefulness, not perfect isolated eyelid motion.",
    "look": "Toward-viewer head/bill orientation is readable. Mild wing/foot/body redraw is visible; still usable as the existing source look pairing at normal91size. No smooth inbetween turn is implied.",
    "codecComparison": "Binary/common63opaque colors+transparent retains silhouette, head turn, eye cue, pale belly and feather pattern. Some soft fringe/detail and fine toe/bill edge pixels are reduced; harder/pixelated edges are visible when enlarged. No major new silhouette or action-read failure at normal91.",
    "feet": "Fine leg/toe groups remain visible; shape changes across source actions and threshold removal mean feet are image regions only. Positive surviving probe pixels do not establish tracked soles, weight, pressure or support."
  },
